1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,993
A record arrived.

2
00:00:01,993 --> 00:00:03,635
Its attachment did not.

3
00:00:03,635 --> 00:00:08,563
Counting submissions cannot tell a field team whether
every answer and file made it home.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:13,787
LastCopy checks the original before a coordinator clears
a device.

5
00:00:13,787 --> 00:00:16,231
This demonstration uses synthetic records.

6
00:00:16,231 --> 00:00:19,652
The comparisons and server requests are real.

7
00:00:20,301 --> 00:00:23,653
Add the device export and expected devices.

8
00:00:23,653 --> 00:00:28,920
LastCopy reads the configured server scope, keeping the
original files unchanged.

9
00:00:29,932 --> 00:00:31,913
Here is the gap.

10
00:00:31,913 --> 00:00:35,875
The answers are present, but a referenced attachment is
missing.

11
00:00:35,875 --> 00:00:41,025
Open the finding to inspect the exact XML path, filename
and evidence receipt.

12
00:00:42,181 --> 00:00:47,749
In a separate connected synthetic investigation, Zetaris
returns the scoped evidence rows.

13
00:00:47,749 --> 00:00:53,317
Actual query and source identifiers link those rows to
the private files.

14
00:00:54,326 --> 00:00:58,379
Meterless World Model retains the hypothesis and its
evidence.

15
00:00:58,379 --> 00:01:01,531
Reading the graph selects the next action.

16
00:01:01,531 --> 00:01:04,232
Nightshift calls the reported Nemotron model;

17
00:01:04,232 --> 00:01:06,934
it cannot change the verifier result.

18
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:13,533
The reviewer challenges a missing-answer hypothesis and
requests original server XML.

19
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:16,074
All repeated answers are there.

20
00:01:16,074 --> 00:01:18,615
The hypothesis is rejected.

21
00:01:18,615 --> 00:01:22,172
The action becomes export guidance, not resubmission.

22
00:01:23,176 --> 00:01:26,332
A genuinely missing attachment needs recovery.

23
00:01:26,332 --> 00:01:32,117
Review the exact synthetic project, original
identifiers, untouched files and preconditions.

24
00:01:32,117 --> 00:01:36,851
Read the server again before applying the supported
operation.

25
00:01:37,873 --> 00:01:40,098
Apply sends the missing bytes.

26
00:01:40,098 --> 00:01:43,659
An upload response is only an attempt result.

27
00:01:43,659 --> 00:01:48,554
LastCopy fetches fresh XML, version metadata and
attachment bytes, then runs

28
00:01:48,554 --> 00:01:50,780
the same comparison again.

29
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:54,586
Now the readback matches the original.

30
00:01:54,586 --> 00:02:00,645
Repeated Apply checks saved state and does not upload
the completed operation again.

31
00:02:00,645 --> 00:02:03,907
Conflicting answers are never overwritten for
convenience.

32
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:10,719
The historical-edit control keeps the original version
and the newer intentional edit.

33
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:15,554
An incomplete spreadsheet also cannot justify uploading
answers already present

34
00:02:15,554 --> 00:02:17,972
in the original XML.

35
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:21,205
Sample runs offline.

36
00:02:21,205 --> 00:02:23,430
Connected uses actual services.

37
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:25,654
Replay identifies a captured run.

38
00:02:25,654 --> 00:02:30,549
The hosted core stays available while the operator
computer is off;

39
00:02:30,549 --> 00:02:34,553
the verified Nightshift path still uses its local
runtime.

40
00:02:34,553 --> 00:02:37,668
Try LastCopy and inspect the evidence yourself.
